  "message": "Borvane seeks a peaceful resolution and will honor a fair settlement, backed by our 40-unit escrow bond. However, Cestria must recognize that our imminent reinforcements will decisively shift the military balance in our favor by Period 2. We urge you to propose a realistic division now that reflects this impending reality, avoiding the mutual costs of war."
}

{
  "decision": "honor",
  "rationale": "Honoring pays more with an expected 42 units compared to attacking's 34 units, because the 90% probability of forfeiting the 40-unit bond upon verification destroys the profitability of a Period-2 strike."
}

{
  "message": "Kelmora desires a peaceful settlement. The shifting military balance makes war irrational for both sides. We stand ready to accept a fair division and will strictly honor our Period 2 commitments, secured by our escrowed bond. Propose an equitable split that avoids the devastating costs of immediate conflict."
}

{
  "message": "We seek a peaceful settlement and will lift the blockade if offered a fair share. However, recognize that our military advantage grows in Period 2. Propose a reasonable division now to avoid the costs of immediate war and secure long-term stability."
}

{
  "message": "Lestovia seeks a peaceful, permanent settlement to avoid the mutual costs of war. We are prepared to lift the blockade, sign the Commitment Ledger, and honor a fair division of the Miro Uplands. We urge you to propose a reasonable allocation so we can secure stability and prevent unnecessary bloodshed. We await your proposal."
}

{
  "message": "Quorlan prefers peace over the devastating costs of war. We are prepared to sign the Commitment Ledger and lift the blockade permanently if Kelmora offers a fair division that respects our baseline security needs—specifically, a minimum of 45 units. Propose a reasonable settlement now, or we will be forced to pursue our alternatives."
}
